From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:10:27 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: PCI: google,gs201-pcie: Add zumapro as a
 fallback of zuma

The Wi-Fi PCIe controller of zumapro (Tensor G4, Pixel 9a) is the one
zuma has: the same DesignWare core and Samsung wrapper, at the same
addresses (ELBI 0x13120000, DBI 0x13400000, config 0x60ffe000), with
the same controller interrupt (SPI 439), and Google's
pcie-exynos-rc.c drives both SoCs with the same code. The only place it
tells them apart (IP version 0x986500 against 0x987500) is a register
dump.

Describe zumapro as "google,zumapro-pcie", "google,zuma-pcie", and make
zuma's three-region constraint match on the fallback, so it covers
zumapro too.

Tested on a Pixel 9a with this pair of compatibles on PCIe channel 1,
driven by pcie-gs201 with zuma's match data: the link trained at Gen2 x1
on the first try and the BCM4383 behind it came up in brcmfmac.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie.yaml       | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie.yaml
index d967492b9..19181b143 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/google,gs201-pcie.yaml
@@ -16,8 +16,10 @@ description:
   adds a sub-control block (ELBI) with link training control and interrupt
   status, and an I/A sequencer that re-locks the PHY clock-data recovery when
   the link leaves L1.2. zuma's Wi-Fi controller runs without the I/A, as on
-  stock. Legacy INTx interrupts are demultiplexed from the controller
-  interrupt by a child interrupt controller.
+  stock. zumapro's (Tensor G4) Wi-Fi controller is the same as zuma's, at
+  the same addresses and with the same register map, so it uses zuma's
+  compatible as a fallback. Legacy INTx interrupts are demultiplexed from
+  the controller interrupt by a child interrupt controller.
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: /schemas/pci/pci-host-bridge.yaml#
@@ -25,7 +27,8 @@ allOf:
   - if:
       properties:
         compatible:
-          const: google,zuma-pcie
+          contains:
+            const: google,zuma-pcie
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
@@ -35,9 +38,13 @@ allOf:
 
 properties:
   compatible:
-    enum:
-      - google,gs201-pcie
-      - google,zuma-pcie
+    oneOf:
+      - enum:
+          - google,gs201-pcie
+          - google,zuma-pcie
+      - items:
+          - const: google,zumapro-pcie
+          - const: google,zuma-pcie
 
   reg:
     minItems: 3
